{
  "schema": "weavec-corpus-expected",
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The corpus ratchet of RFC 0030, section 17.5, written by scripts/corpus-gate.py --update",
    "(or --update-from a results file measured elsewhere, for example by CI). For each platform,",
    "configs.<config> records the per-file compiles (units) and, for wholeProgram configs, the",
    "whole-program analysis (program): errors, warnings, ledger outcome counts,",
    "unresolvedShare.spatialNull, cpuSeconds and workCounters; --full adds traps and --bench",
    "overhead. Counts and shares must match exactly: a worse value fails, and so does a better",
    "one until --update records it. cpuSeconds and overhead may exceed the record by 10% on the",
    "machine that recorded them (not compared elsewhere), work counters by 2%. The platforms stay",
    "empty until the RFC 0030 compiler writes ledgers (S3); legacy holds v0.10.0's numbers for S0",
    "and S1."
  ],
